we begin with a big surprise in  washington on a bill that could affect  americans for generations democratic  senator joe manchin has reversed his  opposition to legislation meant to help  reduce inflation lower prescription drug  costs and fight climate change but  republicans oppose the measure and his  patches is not guaranteed nancy cortes  is at the white house where this bill is  welcome news for president biden nancy  good morning what's on the line here  well vlad simply put this would be the  largest u.s climate change legislation  ever president biden last night declared  it historic it is the product of secret  negotiations over a package that until  yesterday appeared to be dead  two weeks after walking away from a  climate deal west virginia democrat joe  manchin embraced one last night with a  compromise dubbed the inflation  reduction act of 2022. the centerpiece  about 370 billion dollars worth of clean  energy tax incentives and grants  including seventy five hundred dollar  tax credits for many americans who buy  electric cars  the bill would also allow medicare to  negotiate the price of some prescription  drugs and cap out of pocket drug costs  for seniors at two thousand dollars a  year democrats say the cost of all this  would be more than offset by a new  minimum tax on corporations this is a  bill that truly is about fighting  inflation  bringing down costs for families and  putting the country on a sounder  economic footing the motion to concur  with an amendment is agreed to the  surprise deal was announced just hours  after the senate passed a major  bipartisan bill to boost u.s computer  chip production  [Applause]  [Music]  it all comes amid an otherwise gloomy  week of economic news with consumer  confidence down for a third straight  month in the face of record inflation  most families were paying less than two  dollars a gallon at the pump just two  years ago these are not normal times  yesterday the fed hiked short-term  interest rates another three-quarters of  a point in a bid to bring prices back  down as customers and business owners  struggle we are not buying anything  extra we are buying only what we need to  provide the meals that we a lot for it's  the hardest it's ever been to be in  business with every cost going up  and this morning everyone is watching  for the release of the second quarter  gross domestic product numbers typically  if gdp falls for a second quarter in a  row that could signal a looming  recession but the biden administration  has been insisting that that is not the  case this time around that the economy  is simply  recalibrating after a post pandemic boom  nate  nancy thank you
 

